      "writtenOn": "2025-07-21T19:13:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This would belong in a `details` section to explain how this is done.\n\nI would change this message with.\n\n```\nProblem: Within a configuration, an interface can have \"alternate settings\". In this alternate interfaces can be a valid fastboot interface. We currently only look at the default interface which leads to not detecting device properly.\n\nSolution: When inspecting a device, also look at the alternative interface.\n\nDetails: \u003cYou current commit message cleaned up by what is already covered above\u003e.\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 9,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 15,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "bea437ee8236227e2fe1db8f2e6056aa3f7fb5d7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
