        "id": 1083168
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-17T18:27:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since you spent time on Windows and developed a mini-expertise, why not contribute a usb_windows.cpp file to the project :)? Now that Windows ships with WinUSB it is a managable task for a developer of your caliber. \n\nThis would tremendously help `fastboot` (and also `adb`). By fixing it only on macosx you essentially kick that can down the road. It will be up to the fastboot/adb maintainer to write that (if ever) and do their best to test it without your domain knowledge.",
      "parentUuid": "aabd21c6_e9941cc9",
      "revId": "bea437ee8236227e2fe1db8f2e6056aa3f7fb5d7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "daecfc23_88720668",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 2031040
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-18T09:19:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I fully agree that `usb_windows.cpp` would be a great contribution to the `fastboot` client application.\n\nHowever, given constrained resources we have right now (Tomasz is leading implementation of bootloader fastboot on device side and passing security review there, which is P0 for us), would you be OK with filling a bug for implementing `usb_windows.cpp` and having it handled by Tomasz in some less urgent time (let\u0027s agree on finishing this one by the end of Q3 2025)?\n\nThe reason I\u0027m asking for landing `linux` support now and postphoning (a bit) Windows support is that most of the developers in our team are `linux` users (as well as a whole lab infrastructure is linux-based), and timely landing those now is critical for enabling lab infrastructure to work on USB-based solution.",
      "parentUuid": "b86556be_02069ffa",
      "revId": "bea437ee8236227e2fe1db8f2e6056aa3f7fb5d7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
